### Anything else relevant?

- I reproduced it on 20.3.16. I haven't run it on 22.x, but on `main` the karma builder still doesn't set `disableCodeSplitting` (only `unit-test/runners/vitest/build-options.ts` does since #33729). The code path looks unchanged.
- In a real project this showed up as 3–5 component specs failing only when `--include` mixed two folders, while the full suite passed. Which spec happened to call the initialiser first decided the outcome.
- Applying the same `disableCodeSplitting: true` to the karma application build seems like the natural fix, as #33729 did for Vitest.
